## 3. Noncommercial Purpose

A "Noncommercial Purpose" is any purpose that is not intended for or directed
toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation. Without limiting that
definition, the following are commercial and are not Noncommercial Purposes:

(a) selling, renting, leasing, licensing, or otherwise charging anyone for the
software or a derivative work;

(b) offering the software or a derivative work as a paid service, including
software-as-a-service, hosted access, hosting, consulting, or support;

(c) bundling the software or a derivative work into a product, service, or
distribution for which you charge, or that is used to advertise or sell
something else;

(d) use by a for-profit entity in the operation of its business, including
internal use to produce goods or services for sale;

(e) use intended to generate revenue, advertising income, subscription income,
or other commercial benefit.

Use by a charitable organization, educational institution, public research
organization, public safety or health organization, environmental protection
organization, or government institution for its public-interest mission is a
Noncommercial Purpose, regardless of the source of its funding.

